    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechs">Czechs</a> and Slovaks created from the ruins of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> in 1918, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> as its capital.</li><li>Its interwar democracy was the only one in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-europe">Central Europe</a> to last until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich-agreement">Munich Agreement</a> of 1938 dismembered it.</li><li>After 1948 it was a communist state of the Soviet bloc; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/velvet-revolution">Velvet Revolution</a> of 1989 led to its peaceful division in 1992.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bren-light-machine-gun">Bren light machine gun</a> was developed from the Czechoslovak <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zb-vz-26">ZB vz. 26</a>; its name joins <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brno">Brno</a>, where it was designed, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enfield-london">Enfield</a>, where it was made.</p></aside>
    </section>

